<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ali Mughayat Syah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1530">1530</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ali Mughayat Syah was the first sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aceh">Aceh</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumatra">Sumatra</a>, ruling from about 1514 until his death in 1530. He united the north of the island, conquering Pedir and Pasai in the 1520s and driving out the Portuguese who had established themselves there. His conquests made Aceh the leading power of northern Sumatra and a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-malacca">Portuguese Malacca</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ali-mughayat-syah.jpg" alt="Ali Mughayat Syah" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Si Gam Acèh · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jirat_Soleutan_Ali_Mughayat_Syah.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
